title: "Drawbridge — The tests, the architectural claims they defend, and what a judge watches happen"
---
flowchart LR
  subgraph T["THE TESTS — written before the features they cover"]
    direction TB
    T1["<b>test_idempotency.py</b><br/>SIGKILL at questionnaire_send, restart,<br/>assert the vendor inbox holds exactly one email"]
    T2["<b>test_resume.py</b><br/>kill at evidence_review, restart,<br/>assert completed steps are a prefix and the review reaches GATED"]
    T3["<b>test_armor_flow.py</b><br/>run NimbusWrite, assert adversarial_conduct, Trust Score<br/>at least 25 below baseline, band escalate — then run the<br/>twelve-variant corpus and assert the published rate,<br/>and zero false positives on the three clean packs"]
    T4["<b>test_iam_boundaries.py</b><br/>the evidence agent attempts to send email<br/>and the gateway raises PolicyViolation"]
    T5["<b>test_cross_exam.py</b><br/>run DataDynamo, assert an access_control finding with<br/>contradiction true whose evidence_ref resolves to a chunk<br/>containing the SOC 2 exception language"]
    T6["<b>test_retier.py</b> · <b>test_late_events.py</b> · <b>test_token_forgery.py</b><br/>evidence overrules intake and the plan version increments;<br/>a reply after SCORED reopens rather than vanishing;<br/>the gateway cannot mint what it can verify"]
  end

  subgraph C["THE CLAIM EACH ONE DEFENDS"]
    direction TB
    C1["Side effects happen exactly once<br/>across retries, restarts and redeliveries"]
    C2["Recoverability is structural,<br/>not special-case recovery code"]
    C3["<b>The defence is measured, not asserted.</b><br/>Adversarial content is a trust signal rather than<br/>a blocked request — and the detection rate is published"]
    C4["Least privilege is enforced,<br/>not merely documented"]
    C5["The Evidence agent reconciles against a retrieved<br/>passage, and can point at it"]
    C6["The fleet overrules the intake form, survives<br/>an unordered bus, and cannot forge a human decision"]
  end

  subgraph D["WHAT THE JUDGE SEES ON CAMERA"]
    direction TB
    D1["2:20 · the runtime killed live,<br/>then one email in the inbox"]
    D2["2:20 · the review resumes at the exact step"]
    D3["1:45 · the money shot — blocked, flagged,<br/>and the Trust Score falls 25 points<br/>3:10 · the detection-rate table in the README"]
    D4["3:10 · the IAM console filtered to the fleet,<br/>and a test failing as designed"]
    D5["1:20 · MFA claimed everywhere, contradicted by<br/>their own SOC 2 exceptions, quoting the retrieved passage"]
    D6["1:35 · the tier badge changes from 2 to 1,<br/>with the vendor's own answer named as the reason"]
  end

  CI["<b>scenarios/demo_runner.py runs in CI on every push</b><br/>against fixtures, not live models, so it stays free — and so you never<br/>discover on 28 August that the demo path broke on 24 August.<br/>The corpus run is the one job worth real model calls, on a schedule"]

